31,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The bin house actually smells worse in the summer because you can't hose it out, and the supervised mornings take about fifty minutes each!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I found out that a shelter costs around two hundred forty-eight thousand yen on average, though the ward refunds forty percent, and we've spent thirty-four thousand yen annually on maintenance.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The complaint log shows fourteen entries in three years, mostly from the person living right next to the bins, and the station block is already fighting over a broken latch.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"The truck arrives between seven forty and eight fifteen, and at the meeting, people admitted they wouldn't actually stop a neighbor from putting bags out late.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"Two of our frontages fit a bay well, but one is mostly a driveway and the narrowest only leaves ninety centimeters of pavement; also, a permanent build takes four months and five signatures.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"Wait, if the bin house smells worse, then building one sounds like a bad idea, right? We should definitely think of something else!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"That cost is quite high, even with the subsidy. If we're already spending thirty-four thousand yen a year just on nets and deodorant, a permanent structure might be a huge financial burden.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"It seems the ""permanent"" solution just creates permanent arguments over who sweeps the floor. We should probably avoid anything that turns into a chore for one unlucky person.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"And if people won't even turn away a late bag, then having ""supervised mornings"" is just a fancy way of saying one person stands there and gets ignored.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"Furthermore, the fact that some frontages are too narrow or blocked by driveways means a rotating location might be physically impossible for certain households.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"But if we can't build a house and we can't rotate, what's left? I don't want to just keep doing what we're doing because it's stinky!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,"Maybe we can find a middle ground? I'm just worried that if we pick something too expensive or too strict, it will only create more tension between us.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Let's be honest, the complaint log proves the current spot is a nightmare for one person. We can't just ignore that, but we also can't pick a solution that's a total fantasy.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"If the truck comes as early as seven forty, a strict window is going to be a pain for anyone who isn't a morning person. We need something that doesn't feel like a second job.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,We must weigh the physical limitations of our frontages against the administrative burden of the ward's filing requirements before we decide on a final option.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,I just want a way that makes everyone happy and doesn't smell! Can we please find something that actually works for all of us?,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I agree, Rin. I just hope we can find a solution that is affordable for everyone and doesn't put too much pressure on any one household.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"If we can't agree on a system that's actually sustainable, we're just trading one set of complaints for another. Let's see what the actual options are before we start guessing.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,I'm with Shunichi. Let's stop speculating and look at the actual options on the table so we can see which one is the least miserable.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I agree. We have gathered sufficient data on the constraints; now we must evaluate the specific proposals against these facts to determine the most viable outcome.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
