58,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Rin,,"The options are Managed Collection Hours, Rotating Location, or an Enclosed Structure! I don't like the structure because of the smell, so I'm thinking about the others!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Midori,,"The Enclosed Structure seems far too expensive for some of us, and the maintenance sounds stressful, so I'm leaning away from that one too.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Rotating Location seems like the only way to stop the person next to the bins from being the only one complaining, provided the space actually allows it.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,Managed Collection Hours sounds like a nightmare if nobody actually enforces the rules and the truck arrives at seven forty. I'm not voting for that.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Rotating Location is logically the most equitable, but given the frontage measurements, it may be physically impractical for some of us to host the point.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,"If we can't rotate, then maybe the hours are better? But I don't want to stand there for fifty minutes every time it's my turn!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Midori,,"I'm worried that if we rotate, we'll just move the problem around and start arguing about whose driveway is in the way or whose pavement is too narrow.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"That's a fair point, Midori, but staying put just keeps the grudge alive for the person currently stuck with the bins. We need to move the burden, even if it's a bit clunky.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"I'm not into the idea of rotating if it means we're just fighting over who has the ""worst"" spot. But compared to standing on a street corner at 7:40 AM, it's still better.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"If we cannot implement a rotating system due to the narrow frontages, the only remaining logical choice is the structure, despite the costs and administrative delays.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,"But the structure is stinky! I can't vote for that! I think Rotating Location is the most exciting and fair, even if it's a little bit clunky!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I'm still worried about the cost of the structure, but if we rotate, I hope we can all be kind to each other about the space issues.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"I'm voting for Rotating Location. It's the only way to clear the air between neighbors, and we can just figure out the narrow spots as we go.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"I'll go with Rotating Location too. It's not perfect, but it's better than being a glorified security guard for the trash at dawn.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"While the physical constraints are a concern, the other options are either socially unsustainable or financially prohibitive; therefore, I also vote for Rotating Location.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Rin,,I'm voting for Rotating Location too! Let's make it fair for everyone and hope it doesn't smell too bad!,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Midori,,I'll vote for Rotating Location as well. It seems like the best way to keep the peace and keep our costs down.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
